{"author":{"id":"e8ccbc170af88335916e23a1b24e48c04b0a4af82e988d5245cc91e39d6a9e2c"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794497758,"nonce":"n4q7nc5HyGTJoE+BalfwEzJcSD0=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-190c308-integration` (a1242ef..cf5365a).\n\n**Changes**\n- src/ui/input.rs: new. Input card view (URL rows, status chips, shipping box, cost line, preset chips, custom criteria, purpose, Compare button, progress/error line). Compare flow: key check, FX via pick_rate/fetch_rate, Task::run(run_comparison), pipeline event handling, retry. Uruguayan shipping parser. 26 `update` tests.\n- src/ui/mod.rs: ItemStatus, ItemState, RunState, RunError and the Task 12 messages. App now holds items, run, preset, purpose, fx, stale, Arc\u003cSidecarScraper\u003e and a GeminiClient handle that is rebuilt only when key or rpm change. Boot loads the Keychain key and custom presets. View wrapped in a scrollable.\n- src/i18n.rs: 19 new ES/EN keys, all added to Key::ALL.\n- src/ui/snap.rs: DevEnv.gemini_key, read from MAEVE_GEMINI_KEY in debug builds only.\n\n**Gates:** fmt ok · clippy ok · tests ok (164 passed) · scraper-tests n/a\n**Review:** 4 findings — 2 auto, 1 by hand, 1 deferred\n- Shipping box rejects intermediate input per keystroke (\"1.\" reverts, so \"1.500\" can't be typed, and backspace on \"1.500\" is blocked). It follows the acceptance criterion \"invalid shipping input keeping the previous value\". Alternative: store the typed text and flag it invalid, and gate Compare on that.\n- Plan Step 5 (manual end-to-end with two real URLs and a real key) was not run. Set MAEVE_GEMINI_KEY in a debug build, or wait for the Task 14 Settings screen.\n- Snap check was against the demo fixture only. There is no Layout A mockup in the repo, so \"matches Layout A\" was judged against the spec bullets and the token table.\n\n**Decisions**\n- RunState::Error carries RunError (NoApiKey, NotEnoughProducts, Auth, Other(String)) instead of a String, so the message re-translates when the language switches. NoApiKey is the required variant.\n- Compare is two-phase. It sets Running immediately, which blocks double-clicks. It then resolves FX (store cache, then manual setting, then fetch; falls back to a stale automatic rate if offline) and finally starts the pipeline. The Message::FxResolved variant is new.\n- Pipeline item indices refer to non-empty URL rows only, so App keeps a run_items map. Rows are locked while a run is Running.\n- Scraped shipping is a displayed default and is never sent as an override (review finding). ItemState gained shipping_user_set and shipping_invalid. Only user-typed values become shipping_override. The default is recomputed on every view, so it follows FX and settings changes. Shipping is always UYU.\n- Retry(i) re-runs the whole comparison. Ready products are reused, so only failed items are re-scraped.\n- The free-text preset is Preset::Custom with name \"custom\" so history gets a label. Compare is disabled while its criteria are blank.\n- Message::Pipeline wraps a Box\u003cPipelineEvent\u003e to avoid large_enum_variant.\n- Added a debug-only MAEVE_GEMINI_KEY env key and a MAEVE_SCRAPER_DIR override (default CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR/scraper). The Keychain is not read in snapshot runs or tests.\n- Styles (destructive input border, status chip) live in input.rs rather than theme/styles.rs. That file is outside the task's file list.\n- shipping_changed sets stale only when a result exists and never starts a run.","files":null}]}